{"kind":"request","text":"Close dynamic client registration by default\n\nScope: ruling c721a1e9 on 5d56adca, refiled from stale 94f65167. O4 runs\nwith no dynamic registration, and later Workers turn it on only behind\na rate limit.\n\nAdd OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION, a deployment setting, off by default.\nWhen off, POST /oauth/register refuses with a fixed RFC 7591 error\nand writes nothing, and the authorization-server metadata omits\nregistration_endpoint. When it is exactly \"on\", today's behavior holds.\nAny other value closes the OAuth routes, as other invalid OAuth\nsettings do. Metadata-document clients keep working in both states.\n\nDone when tests show both states, the metadata change, a refused\nregistration that writes no row, a metadata-document client still\ncompleting the code flow with registration off, and an invalid value\nclosing the routes, with a frozen gate, the checker's review, and the\nhead on main. Document the setting in docs/mcp.md and\ndocs/security/settings.md.\n\nOrder: next, before O4's Worker deploys.","body":{"conditions":"OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION defaults off, an off Worker refuses registration without a write and omits registration_endpoint, metadata-document clients still complete the flow, an invalid value closes the routes, a frozen gate passes, the checker reviews, and the head lands on main.","target_head":"d7f1ebf7b6246a936fa590d6fbe2c24bbb9c18c8","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}